                <pb facs="0273" n="189" xml:id="pg189"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in 115.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">extracts from constitution.</hi></head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 72. Congress shall assemble in
                    extraordinary session when summoned by the Government. It shall, in such
                    sessions, consider only such business as is specially submitted by the
                    Government for its consideration.</p>
                <p>Paragraph 2 of article 118. To convene Congress in extraordinary sessions for
                    serious reasons of public convenience and after previous consultation with the
                    council of state.</p>
                <p>The preamble of article 118 reads: “The President of the Republic shall exercise
                    the following powers in relation to the legislative department.”</p>
            </div>
